_print_nvidia_egpu_note() {
    cat <<'EOF'

NVIDIA eGPU hotplug configuration:

- The package's module settings may interfere with an internal NVIDIA GPU.
  Override them with /etc/modprobe.d/nvidia-open.conf; an empty file disables
  the module blacklists.

- For a Thunderbolt 4/5 enclosure that is not detected automatically, add this
  line to /etc/modprobe.d/nvidia-egpu.conf:

      options nvidia NVreg_RmForceExternalGpu=1

- To terminate processes using the NVIDIA GPU when it disconnects (useful after
  an unexpected unplug), add this line to /etc/nvidia.env:

      NVIDIA_EGPU_KILL_PROCESSES=1

- For the eGPU ReBAR (nvidia 0000:04:00.0: BAR 1 [mem size 0x10000000 64bit pref]: can't claim; no address assigned) workaround,
  when ReBAR option is set (options nvidia NVreg_EnableResizableBar=1) explicitly - set the sibling bridge BDF in /etc/nvidia.env.
  Its downstream devices are removed during module loading; the handler
  rescans PCI afterward:

      NVIDIA_EGPU_DISABLE_BRIDGE=0000:03:04.0

Keep NVIDIA modules out of the initramfs on eGPU-only systems. Include them
only if the system has an internal NVIDIA GPU.
EOF
}

post_install() {
    _print_nvidia_egpu_note
}

post_upgrade() {
    _print_nvidia_egpu_note
}
